# root crontab for FleetNAS — backup copy.
#
# Root's real crontab lives in /var/spool/cron/crontabs/ on the OS OVERLAY,
# which a UGREEN firmware update can reset. This file lives in ~/repos/scripts,
# which is on the btrfs DATA VOLUME (the RAID array) and survives.
#
# Restore after a firmware update (run ON FleetNAS):
#     sudo crontab ~/repos/scripts/nas/root-crontab
#
# Verify:
#     sudo crontab -l
#
# WARNING: `crontab <file>` REPLACES root's entire crontab. If UGREEN ever adds
# its own root cron entries, check `sudo crontab -l` first and merge rather than
# blindly replacing.
#
# Note the failure mode this guards against: if the crontab is lost, both
# scripts still exist and still work, but nothing runs them — and no email is
# also what "everything is healthy" looks like. The tell is the 05:00 nightly
# going missing, since that one always sends.

*/5 * * * * /home/dhm/repos/scripts/nas/nas-health-monitor.sh 2>&1 | logger -t nas-health-monitor
0 5 * * * /home/dhm/repos/scripts/nas/nas-nightly-summary.sh 2>&1 | logger -t nas-nightly-summary
